{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1830 (owner 2026-11-14: 'better we show a) issue list => a board card, b) my issues (filter by teams at widget creation), c) list of needs you'): HOME SCREEN WIDGETS ×2 (Android Glance app widgets, iOS WidgetKit; web and desktop have none), THE SAME LOOK on both. Model = pure `boardWidget` + `myIssuesWidget` + `needsYouWidget` (src/home-widgets.ts; iOS ExpCore `HomeWidgets.swift`, Android `domain/HomeWidgets.kt`), every mirror replays the `*Cases` comparing the WHOLE object. THREE KINDS (`kinds`, ids are the platform widget kinds): `board` = one board's open issues, the board PICKED when the widget is added (Android: the configure screen lists the active account's boards in sidebar order; iOS: the edit sheet, an AppIntent board parameter); `my-issues` = the viewer's open issues (`assigneeId` = me) in the TEAMS picked when the widget is added (several; none picked = every team); `needs-you` = THE Needs you rows (needs-you.json `needsYou` fold over the active account's synced sessions + digests, every team). OPEN = a status whose category is in `openCategories`. ORDER: `board` = the board's own reading order: category in `categoryOrder` (started first), then the status's sortOrder, then the issue's sortOrder, then identifier; `my-issues` = priority in contract `issuePriority.displayOrder` (urgent first, none last), then updatedAt desc, then identifier. `count` = every matching row (the header's count), `rows` = the first `max` (the platform passes its size's capacity: `capacity` small/medium/large). LOOK (`look`, tokens only, no new component): the platform's widget container filled with the `card` token; HEADER row = the kind's glyph (concept `icons`; `board` = the board's own icon in its color) + the title (type sm, semibold; `board` = the board name, `my-issues` = `copy.myIssues`, `needs-you` = `copy.needsYou`) + the count trailing in muted-foreground (hidden at 0); then ONE-LINE ROWS `rowHeight` high with no dividers: an issue row = THE status icon (category glyph in the status color, as on every issue row) + the title (sm, foreground, truncated) + the identifier trailing (xs, muted-foreground); a needs-you row = its waiting-cards.json glyph (plan `coding-plan`, question `ui-help`, PR `pr-open`) in the needs-you tone + the title + the age trailing (xs muted). No row = ONE muted line centred (`copy.emptyIssues` / `copy.emptyNeedsYou`). Signed out = `copy.signedOut` centred, a tap opens the app. PRIVACY: a needs-you row of an ENCRYPTED chat (its root carries a tree key or a sealed title) reads `copy.sealedRow`, never its card text (the widget snapshot is OS-owned storage, share-targets.json). TAPS (app-shortcuts.json OPENING = the back stack rule): the header = the list in the app (`board` = THE board page, `my-issues` = the Board tab's My issues, `needs-you` = THE Needs you page); an issue row = THE issue page; a needs-you row = its chat by `opens` (needs-you.json). DATA: Android reads the account database in-process (Room) and refreshes on its change (debounced like DirectShareShortcuts); iOS reads a snapshot the app writes into the app group on every change and after sign-in/out, then `WidgetCenter.reloadAllTimelines()`; multi-account: the ACTIVE account.",
